### Justifications of Goal Types

| **Goal** | **Type** | **Why** |
|----------|----------|---------|
| G1, G2, G3, G4, G5, G6 | Perform | All these goals require the robot to *perform* actions that change the world (deliver food, manipulate trays, open doors, etc.). Failure occurs only if no applicable plan can be executed. |
| G4.2.1 | Query | This goal only retrieves information (retrieval capability) without causing an action. |
| G4.2.2, G4.2.3, G4.2.4, G4.2.5 | Perform | They involve coordination, assignment, tracking, and detection—all actions that the robot must execute. |
| G5, G6 | Perform | Both require the robot to *perform* retrieval or door‑opening actions. |

